            "review_title": "Review at Chang Chang Seafood",
            "review_text": "Kim\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam37 contributions\n0\nWorth a visit\nJan 2020 • Couples\nI came here after calling directly to the restaurant as it is quite difficult for us to find somewhere which is still operating in Dong Hoi. Not many options to have lunch here. \nI love the ambience at Chang Chang Seafood. Looks like chilling by the beach. \nEverything here is absolutely great! (Atmosphere, decorations, staff, large portion of food that surprised us ...)\n\nTwo of us just supposed to have lunch, so we ordered 1 bowl of sweet and sour soup, 1 salad, 1 steamed rice and 1 clams soup. But then we couldn't finish all as we never know that would be too much. 😂\n\nHowever, just a little review about the quality of food. I have to admit that all ingredients are perfect, especially I like fresh seafood here (shells, clams, oysters). But still needs some improvement in cooking method to make it more tasty. My soup was not quite yummy though all the oysters and veggies were really nice. As same as my shell salad, the shell was really delicious and fresh, but couldn't mix very well with salad. That was a bit disappointing. Hope my ideas help. 😁\n\nThanks a lot for your hard work. I still recommend people should come here and try!\nRead more\nWritten January 7, 2020",
